w: 1.~They in the Lord that firm- ly trust shall be like Zi- on hill, Which at no time can be re- moved, but stan- deth ev- er still.
w: 2.~As round a- bout Je- ru- sa- lem the moun- tains stand al- way, The Lord his folk doth com- pass so, from hence- forth and for aye.
w: 3.~For ill men's rod up- on the lot of just men shall not lie; Lest right- eous men stretch forth their hands un- to in- iq- ui- ty.
w: 4.~Do thou to all those that be good thy good- ness, Lord, im- part; And do thou good to those that are u- pright with- in their heart.
w: 5.~But as for such as turn a- side af- ter their crook- ed way, God shall lead forth with wi- cked men: on Is- r'el peace shall stay.
